# AWS Cloud Ops Basics

This repository contains foundational AWS Cloud Operations concepts and hands-on examples covering compute, identity & access management, monitoring, and cost optimization.

The purpose of this repository is to demonstrate practical understanding of AWS services commonly used in Cloud Operations / Support roles.

---

## 🔧 Services Covered

- AWS EC2
- AWS S3
- AWS IAM
- AWS CloudWatch
- AWS Cost Optimization basics

---

## 📌 Topics Included

### 1️⃣ EC2 Operations
- EC2 instance launch basics
- Security groups
- Key pairs
- Instance monitoring
- Start/stop & troubleshooting basics

### 2️⃣ IAM Basics
- Users, groups, and roles
- IAM policies (inline & managed)
- Least privilege principle
- IAM best practices

### 3️⃣ Monitoring & Alerts
- CloudWatch metrics
- CloudWatch alarms
- Basic alerting strategy
- Operational monitoring concepts

### 4️⃣ Cost Optimization
- Instance rightsizing
- Storage lifecycle policies
- Cost monitoring basics
- Tagging best practices

---

## 🎯 Target Role

This repository is designed for:
- Cloud Operations Engineer
- Junior Cloud Engineer
- AWS Cloud Support Engineer

